    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Life on Other Planets is the fourth studio album by Supergrass, released on Parlophone in 2002. It marked a confident return after the more mixed reception to their self-titled 1999 album, and it found the band refining their knack for buoyant, melodic rock with a sharper sense of classic British pop and glam influence.\n\nAcross its 40-minute runtime, the album balances brisk power-pop, psychedelic touches, and playful experimentation, with songs that move from punchy guitar work to layered harmonies and keyboard color. Critics generally responded positively, praising its energy and songcraft while noting that it was less tightly focused than the band’s best-known earlier work, but many fans regard it as one of Supergrass’s strongest and most complete records.",
